WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.510 --> 00:00:03.100
I like you just the way you are.

00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:09.680
Imagine you came home from school every day,

00:00:09.680 --> 00:00:11.030
you didn't go on the Internet.

00:00:11.240 --> 00:00:12.930
You didn't play "Flappy Bird,"

00:00:12.930 --> 00:00:14.400
but instead you turned on PBS

00:00:14.400 --> 00:00:17.330
to watch a guy in a cardigan who accepted you no matter what.

00:00:17.780 --> 00:00:19.130
That was Mr. Rogers.

00:00:20.030 --> 00:00:23.180
It's you, I like.

00:00:23.750 --> 00:00:26.550
It's not the things you wear.

00:00:26.550 --> 00:00:27.450
Put on those shoes.

00:00:27.680 --> 00:00:28.350
That sweater.

00:00:28.580 --> 00:00:29.480
He fed his fish.

00:00:29.590 --> 00:00:33.300
"Look at these fish. It's as if they're dancing."

00:00:33.980 --> 00:00:37.350
Watching "Mister Rogers Neighborhood" was kind of like visiting your grandparents,

00:00:37.520 --> 00:00:39.240
except you actually liked going.

00:00:39.240 --> 00:00:41.630
Especially to the neighborhood of make-believe.

00:00:44.780 --> 00:00:48.830
I'm glad you're the way you are.

00:00:48.830 --> 00:00:51.300
I'm glad you're you.

00:00:51.510 --> 00:00:54.230
The show didn't rely on gimmicks to hold your attention.

00:00:54.230 --> 00:00:57.150
The set looked like something you'd make in your basement.

00:00:57.150 --> 00:01:00.080
And the puppets were worn from years of play and affection.

00:01:00.080 --> 00:01:03.000
Showing that you don't need much to have an amazing adventure.

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:04.800
Just a bit of imagination.

00:01:05.700 --> 00:01:07.280
He treated you like an equal.

00:01:07.280 --> 00:01:08.850
"How do I turn your music on here?"

00:01:08.960 --> 00:01:11.100
"Just push play."

00:01:11.100 --> 00:01:12.900
*music starts*

00:01:14.030 --> 00:01:16.050
We learned with them about how crayons are made.

00:01:16.500 --> 00:01:20.330
One of these little boxes has sixteen different color crayons in it.

00:01:20.330 --> 00:01:21.230
Divorce...

00:01:21.230 --> 00:01:23.480
"My mother and dad..."

00:01:23.480 --> 00:01:25.280
"What's wrong with them?"

00:01:25.730 --> 00:01:28.430
They, they fight all the time.

00:01:28.630 --> 00:01:31.350
Fred Rogers never condescended to his audience.

00:01:31.350 --> 00:01:32.930
He simply taught and listened.

00:01:32.930 --> 00:01:36.000
He was the best friend of countless children over the years.

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:38.780
When you watched "Mister Rogers" anything seemed possible.

00:01:39.230 --> 00:01:41.480
895 episodes...

00:01:41.480 --> 00:01:43.050
Four decades...

00:01:43.500 --> 00:01:44.850
One man.

00:01:44.990 --> 00:01:48.000
"It's a beautiful day in this neighborhood..."

00:01:48.900 --> 00:01:54.080
All of us have special ones who have loved us into being.

00:01:54.080 --> 00:01:58.130
Would you just take, along with me,

00:01:58.130 --> 00:02:06.230
10 seconds to think of the people who have helped you become who you are.

00:02:06.230 --> 00:02:08.930
"Won't you be my neighbor?"

00:02:09.380 --> 00:02:11.850
"Hi, Neighbor."

